+## Failed session startup
+
+- A `beforeSession` that throws an `Error` rejects the caller with that same error and runs `onError(session, error)` followed by `afterSession(session)`; the turn stops before user-input hooks, provider interaction, or tool execution ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L40)).
+- `afterSession` runs even when allocation in `beforeSession` only partially completed, so cleanup must track which resources were acquired and tolerate missing resources; receiving this hook does not imply startup succeeded, and the engine adds no startup-success flag ([validated by: releases a partial allocation when beforeSession rejects](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.cleanup.test.ts#L8)).
+
 ## Engine startup
 
 - The engine's `start()` method rejects the returned promise when it cannot bind the configured port, rather than emitting an unhandled error event that would take the process down ([validated by: rejects instead of taking the process down with an unhandled error event](../../src/config.test.ts#L174)).
 
